<article class="env-definition" id="0702">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0702">Definition <span data-tag="0702">46.8.5</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Let $M$ be an $A$-module. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
A <em>pure projective resolution</em> $P_\bullet \to M$ is a universally exact sequence 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to P_1 \to P_0 \to M \to 0  \]
</div>
<p>
 with each $P_ i$ pure projective. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
A <em>pure injective resolution</em> $M \to I^\bullet $ is a universally exact sequence 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  0 \to M \to I^0 \to I^1 \to \ldots  \]
</div>
<p>
 with each $I^ i$ pure injective. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>